                <pb facs="0475" n="371" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg371"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4254: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-17T21:00:00+08:00">February 17, 1932—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 17—11:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>65. Japanese Consul Iguchi stated tonight
                    that the Consulate General expected momentarily from Tokyo terms of an ultimatum
                    requiring the immediate cessation of hostilities and withdrawal on the part of
                    Chinese Army; that the Japanese Consul would immediately deliver same to Mayor
                    and Japanese Army commander to Chinese Army commander. Iguchi opined that the ultimatum would be
                    delivered tonight and 24 [hours?] would be given for compliance.</p>
                <p>Repeated to the Legation and Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
